      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "threshold = int(input())\nn = int(input())\nmeasurements = [int(value) for value in input().split()]\nlast_transmitted = measurements[0]\ntransmitted = [last_transmitted]\n\nfor index in range(1, n):\n    measurement = measurements[index]\n    if abs(measurement - last_transmitted) >= threshold:\n        transmitted.append(measurement)\n        last_transmitted = measurement\n\nprint(*transmitted)\n",
      "statement": "Given an integer [[threshold]] and a sequence of integer measurements, output the values transmitted by the following rule.\n\nAlways transmit the first measurement. Then process the remaining measurements in input order. Transmit a measurement only if its absolute difference from the <<last transmitted measurement>> is <<greater than or equal to>> [[threshold]].\n\nAn ignored measurement does not change the reference. A transmitted measurement becomes the new reference.\n\nFor example, with [[threshold]] = {{5}}, the measurements {{10 12 15 13 9 4 6}} produce {{10 15 9 4}}. The value {{12}} is ignored, so {{15}} is compared with {{10}}.",
